# The day-reveal page is hand-built markup, not generated from this file --
# the build skips *-seed.cho. This is the editable source of that verse;
# tools/twelve-days.py folds it back into site/songs/twelve-days-of-christmas.qmd.
#
# The band: the chords are written once. The grid has one row for each line of
# the verse, in the same order, and each day is played as the two opening rows
# and then the rows of the gifts sung that day. Every row names its own meter,
# since the rows are put together differently each day.
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{style: carol}
{comment: The verse}
{start_of_grid}
| 4/4 D . Bm . |
| 4/4 Em A D . |
| 3/4 A |
| 3/4 A |
| 3/4 A |
| 3/4 A |
| 3/4 A |
| 3/4 A |
| 3/4 A |
| 4/4 D . E . | A |
| 3/4 D |
| 3/4 Bm |
| 4/4 E . A . |
| 4/4 D/F# G D/A A | D |
{end_of_grid}
On the [D]first day of [Bm]Christmas,
My [Em]true love [A]sent to [D]me
[A]Twelve drummers drumming,
[A]Eleven pipers piping,
[A]Ten lords a-leaping,
[A]Nine ladies dancing,
[A]Eight maids a-milking,
[A]Seven swans a-swimming,
[A]Six geese a-laying,
[D]Five [E]golden [A]rings,
[D]Four calling birds,
[Bm]Three French hens,
[E]Two turtle [A]doves,
And a [D/F#]partr[G]idge [D/A]in a [A]pear [D]tree!
